<p>Worth being clear about what hasn''t changed: Finland still has no domestic B2B e-invoicing mandate of any kind, and none is currently scheduled. Businesses with turnover above €10,000 have a statutory right under the 2019 eInvoicing Act to demand e-invoices from their suppliers, and B2B adoption is genuinely widespread as a result — but nothing requires a business to issue them. The only firm future date on Finland''s e-invoicing horizon is the EU''s ViDA deadline of 1 July 2030, for intra-EU B2B transactions specifically, and Finland has indicated it plans to implement at that point rather than moving earlier the way several of its EU neighbours are choosing to.</p>
<p><strong>What this means for your team:</strong> if you supply Finnish Central Government specifically, confirm your ordering process — not just your invoicing — is genuinely Peppol Advanced Ordering compatible, since this is a step beyond what most B2G mandates in this tracker require. For everything else in Finland, don''t wait for a domestic B2B mandate that doesn''t currently exist — if your counterparties expect e-invoices contractually, that expectation is the real driver here, not a statutory deadline.</p>');
